extends ../../../layouts/master.pug

block title
  title Our Mission, Vision, and Values | Nazarene Bible College
  meta(name='description', content='Learn about Nazarene Bible College’s mission, vision, identity, and core values rooted in Wesleyan-Holiness theology and ministry preparation.')

block header
  include ../../../components/header.pug

block content
  section.section-box
    .banner-hero.nav-breadcrums.bg-gray-100
      .container
        .breadcrumb
          ul
            li.home
              a(href='/') Home
            li
              a(href='/about/') About
            li
              span Purpose &amp; Mission

  section.section-box
    .banner-hero.banner-head-image(style='background: url(/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_560002892.jpeg); background-size: cover; background-position: center center;')
      .container
        .text-center
          h1.text-heading-1.color-white.mt-30
            | Purpose &amp; Mission

  section.section-box.mt-50.mb-50
    .container
      .row
        .col-lg-2
        .col-lg-8.text-center
          h2#mission.text-heading-2.color-gray-900 Mission
          p.text-body-lead-large.color-gray-600.mt-30
            | Nazarene Bible College exists to glorify Jesus Christ as Lord by preparing adults to evangelize, disciple, and minister to the world.
        .col-lg-2

  .section-box.mt-40
    .container
      .row
        .col-lg-1
        .col-lg-10
          .box-image
            img.img-responsive.bdrd-16(src='/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_809103813.jpeg', alt='Supporting image for mission and vision')
        .col-lg-1

  section.section-box.mt-80.mb-50
    .container
      .row
        .col-lg-2
        .col-lg-8.text-center
          h2#vision.text-heading-2.color-gray-900 Vision
          p.text-body-lead-large.color-gray-600.mt-30
            | To be widely regarded by alumni, pastors, districts and churches as a trustworthy partner providing the highest-quality, most-accessible, lowest-cost ministry preparation to adults.
        .col-lg-2

  section.section-box.mt-50.mb-50
    .container
      +ContentRightImageLeft('/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_116912183.jpeg')
        .content-detail
          h2#identity.text-heading-2 Identity
          p.text-body-text.mt-30
            | Nazarene Bible College is an undergraduate, professional school of Christian ministry committed to academic and practical programs designed to educate students for service and leadership in a diverse world.
          p.text-body-text.mt-20
            | Founded and sponsored by the Church of the Nazarene in 1967, the college has a unique place among the institutions of higher learning in the denomination. The college provides ministerial preparation for a diverse community of adult learners primarily within the United States. The college is committed to a strong program of academic excellence offering baccalaureate and associate degrees supported by appropriate student development programs and strategies.
          p.text-body-text.mt-20
            | Nazarene Bible College views truth through the Wesleyan-Holiness perspective and affirms the Bible as the cornerstone for a proper understanding of God&rsquo;s redemptive plan for humankind. The college especially emphasizes the biblical doctrine of entire sanctification and living a holy, Christlike life.

  section.section-box.mt-50.mb-30
    .container
      .row
        .col-lg-2
        .col-lg-8.text-center
          h2#core-values.text-heading-2.color-gray-900 Core Values
          p.text-body-lead-large.color-gray-600.mt-30
            | The following core values express our finest aspirations and serve as guiding principles in the pursuit of our mission to equip students for effective Christian ministry.
        .col-lg-2

  section.section-box.pt-20.pb-50
    .container
      .row
        .col-lg-4.col-md-12.col-sm-12
          .list-icons.mt-30
            .item-icon.none-bd
              span.icon-left
                img(src='/assets/imgs/page/homepage2/icon-acquis.svg', alt='')
              h3.text-heading-4 Learning and Instruction
              p.text-body-text.color-gray-600.mt-15
                | We acknowledge the inspired truth of Scripture as the reference point for our educational process. We seek to develop lifelong learners with a Christian worldview. We are committed to academic and professional excellence. We desire to achieve balance in our curriculum through the integration of intellectual, spiritual and practical studies with a foundation in the Wesleyan-Holiness theology.
        .col-lg-4.col-md-12.col-sm-12
          .list-icons.mt-30
            .item-icon.none-bd
              span.icon-left
                img(src='/assets/imgs/page/homepage2/icon-active.svg', alt='')
              h3.text-heading-4 Personal Development
              p.text-body-text.color-gray-600.mt-15
                | We hold that theological education involves shaping the whole person. Therefore, we value the development of moral and ethical integrity, physical and emotional health, and spiritual maturity, all as the demonstration of character through a holy lifestyle.
        .col-lg-4.col-md-12.col-sm-12
          .list-icons.mt-30
            .item-icon.none-bd
              span.icon-left
                img(src='/assets/imgs/page/homepage2/icon-retent.svg', alt='')
              h3.text-heading-4 Service and Mission
              p.text-body-text.color-gray-600.mt-15
                | We prepare students to engage in practical ministry. We value the demonstration of leadership and servanthood to meet the spiritual and social needs of our world and therefore, our curriculum emphasizes a multicultural awareness in missional service. We encourage interdependence with local churches and diverse ministry contexts where our students can utilize their gifts and graces for service to the church and to the world.
